    "field": "Ion-induced atmospheric nucleation",
    "problem": "Accurately assessing the link between solar activity and climate is challenging because the mechanisms and significance of ion-induced aerosol nucleation, driven by cosmic rays, and its subsequent influence on cloud formation remain poorly understood and quantified.",
    "method": "This paper provides a comprehensive overview of theoretical, modeling, laboratory, and field work to assess the role and relevance of ions in the formation of tropospheric aerosol particles and their subsequent effects on clouds and climate.",
    "task": "The task is to provide an overview of theoretical, modeling, laboratory, and field work on the role and relevance of ions for the formation of new aerosol particles in the troposphere and the subsequent effects on clouds.",
